^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\operatorname{sech} }^{2}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545757 17592186576411 true] [17592186514374 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{-2}}-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{2}^{-2}-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{1}{4}-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(-\\frac{15}{4})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545757 17592186576411 false] [17592186514374 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{-2}}-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{2}^{-2}-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\left(\\frac{1}{4}-4\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\left(-\\frac{15}{4}\\right)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545757 17592186576411 true] [17592186514381 1074 "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\