hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}r\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545757 17592186576411 true] [17592186537906 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/56/5673a3eadfa3c01dbb9e2c8bf497b17f34a834d950621afa7d480af625ce1e18.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=xy+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,dx+(xy+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)]\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y)=y.$" 13194139545757 17592186576411 false] [17592186537906 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}\\left(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\right)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/56/5673a3eadfa3c01dbb9e2c8bf497b